{"text": "The impression of authenticity about a person results from an evaluation by the perceiver that the information derived from that person can be used to take adaptive decisions. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Such information is available through two categories of indicators, cues and signals. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Cues are features of the environment that have not necessarily evolved for communication purposes but that nonetheless convey information. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> In other words, a social cue is an opportunity for receivers to extract information about an individual, possibly with the aid of contextual indicators and some basic rules about the relationships between these indicators. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> The second source of information about individuals is social signals. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Social signals are actions or structures that evolved as a result of their effect on other organisms. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Even though signals might not always contain information, or act in the benefit of the receiver, signaling is expected to be reliable whenever the costs of deceptive signals exceed the benefits of providing honest cues.", "alignment": {"characters": ["T", "h", "e", " ", "i", "m", "p", "r", "e", "s", "s", "i", "o", "n", " ", "o", "f", " ", "a", "u", "t", "h", "e", "n", "t", "i", "c", "i", "t", "y", " ", "a", "b", "o", "u", "t", " ", "a", " ", "p", "e", "r", "s", "o", "n", " ", "r", "e", "s", "u", "l", "t", "s", " ", "f", "r", "o", "m", " ", "a", "n", " ", "e", "v", "a", "l", "u", "a", "t", "i", "o", "n", " ", "b", "y", " ", "t", "h", "e", " ", "p", "e", "r", "c", "e", "i", "v", "e", "r", " ", "t", "h", "a", "t", " ", "t", "h", "e", " ", "i", "n", "f", "o", "r", "m", "a", "t", "i", "o", "n", " ", "d", "e", "r", "i", "v", "e", "d", " ", "f", "r", "o", "m", " ", "t", "h", "a", "t", " ", "p", "e", "r", "s", "o", "n", " ", "c", "a", "n", " ", "b", "e", " ", "u", "s", "e", "d", " ", "t", "o", " ", "t", "a", "k", "e", " ", "a", "d", "a", "p",